# Content

## Post formats

There are exactly three post types. Each goes in `src/content/posts/`
(or your equivalent collection) with frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: "On the quietness of tools"
date: 2026-05-22
type: essay        # essay | linked | notes | review
tags: [tools, typography]
star: true         # essays may be "starred originals"; linked posts never are
linkUrl: "…"       # required when type: linked, omitted otherwise
linkAuthor: "…"    # optional, attributes the linked piece
---
```

### Type rules

- **essay** — original long-form. Eligible for `star: true`.
- **linked** — points outward. Must include `linkUrl`. Body: one-paragraph
  lede + a single `<blockquote>` excerpt from the source + one or two
  sentences of commentary. Do **not** restate the linked piece.
- **notes** — short observations. One to three paragraphs. No quotes.
- **review** — review of a product, book, film. Verdict-first, body
  underneath. Use sparingly.

## Voice

- First person singular. Past tense for narrative, present for reflection.
- No "I think", "in my opinion", "I believe" — the post is on your blog;
  ownership is implicit.
- Avoid em-dashes-as-comma; use real em-dashes for parentheticals only.
- Numbers under ten written as words. "Three notes", not "3 notes".
- Inline links use Markdown: `[anchor text](url)`. Anchor text is a
  natural noun phrase, never "click here" or the bare URL.
- Quoted speech uses curly quotes. So do apostrophes.

## UI copy

- Nav items lowercase prefixed with `/`: `/latest`, `/archive`, etc.
- Page eyebrows match the URL path (`/sponsor`, `/archive`).
- Section headings are uppercase mono, two or three words.
- Button copy is sentence-case, ends with an arrow: `Reserve a week →`.
- Footer always reads `© <year> R. Park` on the left, `ripblog · <route>`
  on the right.

## Don'ts

- No emoji anywhere — not in posts, not in UI, not in commit messages
  rendered in the UI.
- No exclamation points in your own voice. Quoted speech is fine.
- No marketing words: "delightful", "seamless", "revolutionary", "AI",
  "thoughtful experience". They cheapen the page.
- No "Welcome to…" intros, ever.
